     4	 * These are plain numbers rather than Tailwind width classes, because two
     5	 * measurements made the classes lie about their own size:
     6	 *
     7	 * 1. NativeWind resolves `1rem` to React Native's 14pt on native, not to a
     8	 *    browser's 16px. `w-12` is therefore 42pt, not the 48 its name implies —
     9	 *    every register column was 12.5% narrower than the code claimed, and the
    10	 *    role header (`w-12`, 42pt) sat 6pt left of the role cells under it
    11	 *    (`width: 48`). Points here mean points.
    12	 * 2. Text grows with the reader's iOS text size. A phone set to xxLarge scales
    13	 *    every font by 1.235, so a 10pt header renders at 12.35pt: measured off a
    14	 *    screenshot from that phone, "OVR" plus its arrow wanted 46.9pt of a 42pt
    15	 *    column and the arrow was clipped to a 1pt sliver.
    16	 *
    17	 * So every width below is derived rather than chosen: it holds its own header
    18	 * at the largest size that header is allowed to reach, plus the sort arrow,
    19	 * plus a gutter to the column beside it. `squad-register-columns.test.ts`
    20	 * re-runs that arithmetic, so a width cannot quietly stop fitting again.
    21	 */
    22	
    23	/**
