   103	
   104	## Decision log (locked through 2026-08-06)
   105	
   106	| Decision | Choice |
   107	|---|---|
   108	| Match involvement | Matches auto-play and powers always fire automatically in their authored context — there is no manual hero tap. The player's live controls are Formation, Playstyle, Swap, and Energy Use |
   109	| Match effort | Playstyle controls tactical intent; Save Energy / Balanced / All Out controls physical effort, movement, and condition drain without directly changing passing or shooting |
   110	| Career structure | Climb from D5 · District League to D1 · Global League; win **both** D1 and the Hero Cup to complete the main journey, then continue endlessly; the career record is kept in the Hall of Fame |
   111	| Business model | Paid app, ~$0.99, no IAP at launch; economy balanced purely for fun |
   112	| Art direction | B+ "heroic chibi" pixel art + comic FX layer + broadcast match dressing |
   113	| Opening music | **“Heroes Start Here”** — original 128 BPM title-screen fanfare and seamless chiptune loop |
   114	| Match music | **“Match Day Heroes”** — original 128 BPM heroic stadium-chiptune loop; the official watched-match theme |
   115	| Management music | **“Clubhouse Dreams”** — original 112 BPM warm chiptune loop for training, squad, transfers, facilities, and finances |
   116	| Event music | **“The Big Call”** — original 136 BPM dramatic chiptune loop for story interruptions and player choices |
   117	| Awakening music | A 10.3-second trimmed **“Spirit of the Dead”** pre-rise bed starts with the limp and fades over its final second if the player waits; it cuts the instant the rise begins, when the existing angels/harps ascension cue takes over |
   118	| Income sources | All four: sponsors, tickets/fans, prize money, player sales |
   119	| Supporters | Wins and heroes who actually appear add supporters; only the third and later consecutive losses cause slow decline, and a draw or win resets the streak |
   120	| Managed sponsors | D5 retains automatic income; 1/2/3 selectable slots unlock permanently at D4/D3/D2, with monthly payments and league objectives but no signing or unlock perks |
   121	| Buzz | Season 3 unlocks Buzz from wins, goals, and distinct hero power moments; it pays sponsor cash at Weeks 15 and 30, then resets |
   122	| Currencies | Money + Training Points (TP) — each with exactly one job |
   123	| Contract talks | Offer/counter with mood meter; a light card mini-game influences (max ±20%) but never fully decides |
   124	| Superpower acquisition | Flat 10% post-match awakening check (3-match cooldown, wage stays locked until renewal) + rare expensive pre-powered signings; chance events never award powers *(corrected 2026-08-05 — this entry previously described the rejected risky-chance-event design)* |
   125	| Hero field limit | "Hero License" slots: 2 on the pitch at start, up to 4 via club prestige; squad ownership uncapped |
   126	| Salaries | Weekly wages for everyone; raises at contract renewal; hero-rate renewals (×3–5) after awakening |
   127	| Players | Fictional, procedurally generated (no licensing risk); gentle aging with retirement and a legacy system |
   128	| Stack | Expo/React Native + TypeScript + react-native-skia (Atlas API); deterministic pure-TS sim core |
   129	
   130	### Balance decisions (2026-07-25–29, implementation campaign complete)
   131	
   132	The scale-invariant campaign replaces compressed high ratings with ratio-based
   133	contests, a bounded pace curve, an honest D5→D1 ladder, and percentage-based
   134	rival growth. The locked implementation spec and completed acceptance evidence are
   135	in [the scale-invariant attributes master spec](docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-29-scale-invariant-attributes.md).
   136	
   137	| Question | Decision | Where it lands |
   138	|---|---|---|
   139	| Economy: cut wages or raise income? | **Raise income**, via the fans / ticket price / sponsor levers | Division income scales; transfer values and generated wages are anchored to each division's support band |
   140	| Should PAC matter? | **Yes.** Pace must convert into chances — accepting it as a dead stat is rejected | `PACE_SPEED128` supplies bounded, strictly increasing movement with fixed-point residue carry |
   141	| Is the goalkeeper the most important player? | **No.** Flatten the shot/save asymmetry so the eleven matter roughly equally | REF now uses the symmetric log-ratio contest and each division has an explicit keeper REF target |
   142	| Opponent shape | **Balanced teams with visible specialists.** | Explicit support, specialist focus, pace, and keeper tables replace the old star back-solve |
   143	| Opponent season scaling | **Slow percentage growth**, so the meaning is stable at every division | Cozy +3%/season, Chairman +4%, deterministic stochastic rounding, capped below 999 |
   144	| Tutorial fixture | Open against the **strongest** rival, then ease down to the weakest by match five | `schedule.ts` `pinOpeningLeagueOpponents` |
   145	| Hero worth | **Powers are typed spectacle after ordinary ratios.** | Power bonuses use d64, multiplier, geometry, or time effects rather than hidden raw-stat additions |
   146	| Chairman mode | **Genuinely harder**, not Cozy with four economic knobs turned down | `difficulty.ts` needs a difficulty axis beyond the economy |
   147	| How hard is D5? | **1 season for a good player, 2 at most for someone still learning.** Not a multi-season tutorial arc, and never the current unsignposted permanent 10th place | Sets the target for every number above |
   148	| Should the harness gate the ramp? | **Yes** — assert a best-play career promotes out of D5 **within 2 seasons**, and that a competent-play career manages it in 1 | `division-ramp-probe.test.ts` (`DIVISION_RAMP_PROBE=1`). Not `m2-balance.test.ts`: it scores fixtures from the seed alone and never reads squad strength |
   149	| Manual Zone tap | **Removed permanently**; powers always fire automatically | Done — see docs/04 |
   150	| Cup giant-killing | **Enabled:** one division down wins 5–10%; two-plus down wins 1–2% | Deterministic long-tail Cup model; Bert celebrates every qualifying player win with gap-specific copy |
   151	| Financial Report (2026-08-06) | The post-match summary is the **Financial Report**: slot-reel reveals, seeded ±10% gate/merch variance with a 1-in-10 surge band (+11–20%), facility base × multiplier beats, pixel surge banners | Spec + plan council-audited; variance only on report-eligible settlements; projections stay baseline ("typical") |
   152	
   153	## Deliberately deferred (not forgotten)
   154	
   155	- Sprite squash-and-stretch on kicks — cut 2026-08-05 (struck from doc 08's juice budget): the Atlas batched renderer only applies uniform RSXform scale, so it cannot express non-uniform squash. If revived, ship it as pre-authored squashed/stretched kick frames selected on PASS/SHOT events — a frame swap fits the Atlas pipeline
   156	- Final mix balance — decide during M4 polish
   157	- PC input mapping and landscape layouts — decide at the PC port spike
   158	- Localization beyond English — post-launch
   159	- Android release timing — after iOS beta feedback

