   426	| 5 | Sponsor contract snapshot `offerLine` | `:510` | **`strictObject`** | Carries `sponsorContentId` (`:508`) — id lookup works |
   427	| 6 | Sponsor offer snapshot `offerLine` | `:527` | **`strictObject`** | Carries `sponsorContentId` (`:525`) |
   428	| 7 | Sponsor **rules** `brands[].offerLine`, `objectives[].labelTemplate` | `:458`, `:483`; snapshotted whole at `:1283` | **`strictObject`** | Content copied into the save |
   429	| 8 | `pendingEvent.outcomeText` | `:758` | optional | Resolved event prose. Sibling `resolvedOutcomeIndex` (`:759`) already persists — the key fix is nearly free |
   430	| 9 | `pendingCupGiantKillingCelebrations[].title`, `.body` | `:1343-1348` | `.passthrough()` | Four authored Bert speeches from `game/cup-giant-killing.ts:17-46`, persisted whole |
   431	| 10 | `seasonRecap.cupResult` | `:1176` | free string | Mixes `'Not entered'` / `'Winners'` / `'Entered'` with round labels (`game/season-recap.ts:247-257`); rendered as a panel **title** at `SeasonEndScreen.tsx:166` |
   432	| 11 | `playerRequestRules.requests[].title`, `.line` | `:429-436` | `.passthrough()` | Content rules copied into the save |
   433	
   434	`sponsorName` and club names on these schemas are names, not prose, and are not
   435	translated (§10).
   436	
   437	**One rendering rule covers all eleven:** a persisted snapshot renders through a
   438	content-id or key lookup; the stored English is the legacy fallback for careers
   439	saved before this change. Surfaces 5–7 and 11 already persist the content id
   440	they came from, so their lookup needs no new field at all — only a renderer that
   441	prefers the id over the frozen string.
   442	
   443	`seasonRecap.cupResult` (10) is the awkward one: it is a *denormalised* string
   444	that mixes an outcome word with a round label, and §3's claim that "cup round
   445	labels are already an enum" covers `rounds[].label` but not this sibling. It
   446	becomes a `{ outcome, round }` pair rendered at the UI.
   447	
   448	**Two rules the implementation must not get wrong:**
   449	
   450	1. **Always dual-write.** `label` stays `nonemptyString` and stays **required**.
   451	   New rows write the English `label` *and* `labelKey` + `labelParams`. A writer
   452	   that emits only keys fails validation on its own schema. The UI prefers
   453	   `labelKey` and falls back to `label`.
   454	2. **`labelParams` carries raw values, never formatted text.** Store
   455	   `{ fee: 240000 }`, not `{ fee: "$240,000" }`. Formatting is a display concern
   456	   (§3.4) — preformatting freezes one locale's thousands separator and currency
   457	   placement into SQLite, which is the exact bug this section exists to prevent.
   458	   Note `career.ts:836-1004` shows `labelParams` must also carry *names* —
   459	   sponsor, player, facility — and that `FACILITY_CATALOG[...].name` needs keys
   460	   of its own.
   461	
   462	**On schema versions, precisely.** Adding *optional* `labelKey` / `labelParams`
   463	fields to the four `strictObject` schemas requires new schema declarations but
   464	**no `GAME_SCHEMA_VERSION` bump and no migration rung** — old saves parse
   465	unchanged, because nothing has to be synthesised for them (the ladder at
   466	`game-state-codec.ts:2764-2786` exists for that case, and this is not that
   467	case). An earlier draft said "needs a codec schema bump", which was ambiguous
   468	and is corrected here.
   469	
   470	Do **not** relax those `strictObject` schemas to `.passthrough()` to avoid
   471	thinking about it. Silently dropping unknown keys is worse than a declaration.
   472	
   473	**Event outcomes have no ids, and that is a trap.** Outcomes in
   474	`content/events.json` are anonymous weighted entries (`weight`, `text`,
   475	`successHeadline`) with no `id`. Keying their translations by array index means
   476	a future reordering silently reassigns every translated outcome to the wrong
   477	event branch — a corruption that no CI gate above would catch, because every
   478	key would still resolve. **Add explicit `id` fields to event outcomes in
   479	Phase 1**, before any outcome is translated. A frozen-order CI assertion is the
   480	weaker alternative and should only be taken if adding ids proves to break
   481	something.
   482	
   483	## 5. The language picker
   484	
   485	**Primary placement: the sign-your-first-player screen**
   486	(`CharacterCreationScreen`). It already hosts a difficulty radio group in a
   487	`PaperPanel`, so a Language panel sits alongside it with the same furniture:
   488	
   489	```
   490	┌ Language ────────────────── English ┐
   491	│  ● English                          │
   492	│  ○ Español                          │
   493	│  ○ Português (Brasil)               │
   494	│  ○ Français                         │
   495	│  ○ Deutsch                          │
   496	│  ○ Bahasa Indonesia                 │
   497	│  ○ Tiếng Việt                       │
   498	└─────────────────────────────────────┘
   499	```
   500	
   501	- Each language is written **in itself**, never "Spanish".
   502	- **"Tiếng Việt" cannot render in Silkscreen** — it contains `ế` and `ệ`, two of
   503	  the glyphs §4.1 proves are missing. That one row must draw in the Vietnamese
   504	  face (or the `body` face) **in every locale**, or the picker itself exhibits
   505	  the mid-word typeface substitution this whole section exists to prevent. The
   506	  row is a per-language literal, so it carries its own face rather than
   507	  inheriting the active one.
   508	- English is preselected. First launch may *suggest* the device language by
